{
  "grouping_reason": "Single Sysmon Event 1 on LAPTOP-HR03 at 09:32:14 MYT under CORP\\hr.user: powershell.exe spawned by explorer.exe with commandLine 'powershell.exe -NoProfile -WindowStyle Hidden -Command \"Import-Module ExchangeOnlineManagement; Connect-ExchangeOnline -ShowBanner:$false; New-InboxRule -Mailbox hr.user@corp.local -Name `Payroll Sync` -From `noreply@corp-payroll.com` -MoveToFolder `RSS Subscriptions` -StopProcessingRules $true\"'. Three stacked anomalies: (a) the -NoProfile -WindowStyle Hidden flag pair = automation context, not an interactive admin shell — there is no visible PowerShell window and no user profile loaded; (b) the user CORP\\hr.user is a regular HR end-user, not a mailbox/Exchange administrator — there is no operational role-based reason for an HR user to be running the ExchangeOnlineManagement module; (c) the New-InboxRule parameters are an email-hiding signature: move emails FROM the corporate payroll-notification address (noreply@corp-payroll.com) INTO 'RSS Subscriptions' (a folder users rarely check) with StopProcessingRules=true (no further inbox rules will process these messages). Typical SOC failure mode: 'PowerShell is signed Microsoft binary, no malware indicator, must be admin maintenance' or 'a single inbox rule is benign mailbox config'.",
